<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Kurundwad Junior</h1><p class="st-meta">1855 CE – 1948 CE · capital Kurundwad</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The junior of two Patwardhan Brahmin states at Kurundwad, formed by the division of 1855.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patwardhan">Patwardhan</a> holding of Kurundwad, created in the family partition of 1811, was divided in 1855 between two branches, and the Junior branch received its own scattered villages.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Kurundwad Junior was a small state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-maratha-country">Southern Maratha Country</a>, later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-states-agency">Deccan States Agency</a>, sharing the town of Kurundwad with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kurundwad-senior">Kurundwad Senior</a>. Little else of its history is recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> Kurundwad Junior was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bombay-state">Bombay State</a> in 1948 and has been part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a> since 1960, in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kolhapur-state">Kolhapur</a> district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kurundwad-junior.jpg" alt="Kurundwad Junior" width="320" height="174"><figcaption>Image: Robert Alfers · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KIurundwadjr_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1855 CE – 1948 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kurundwad</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Marathi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kurundwad State (Junior)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1902&amp;focus=kurundwad-junior" aria-label="Kurundwad Junior on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6711 1558 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kurundwad Junior lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7031 1814L7031 1814M7031 1814L7364 1601M7031 1814L7364 1602M7031 1814L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7031 1814h0M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7031 1814h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7031 1814h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1902&amp;focus=kurundwad-junior">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
